%S A002010 14,560,11200,197568,3378944,57573888,986442752,17048894464,
%T A002010 297480323072,5239685947392,93114988068864,1668499560824832,
%U A002010 30125902436302848,547757493760557056,10023463373662584832,184500750142293147648,3414455636006975569920,63504001472085475983360
%N A002010 Number of rooted planar maps with 2n trivalent vertices and a root vertex of valence 8.
%D A002010 R. C. Mullin, E. Nemeth and P. J. Schellenberg, The enumeration of almost cubic maps, pp. 281-295 in Proceedings of the Louisiana Conference on Combinatorics, Graph Theory and Computer Science. Vol. 1, edited R. C. Mullin et al., 1970.
%D A002010 N. J. A. Sloane, A Handbook of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1973 (includes this sequence).
%D A002010 N. J. A. Sloane and Simon Plouffe, The Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1995 (includes this sequence).
%H A002010 Christopher Smolen, <a href="/A002010/b002010.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..200</a>
%H A002010 R. C. Mullin, E. Nemeth and P. J. Schellenberg, <a href="/A002005/a002005.pdf">The enumeration of almost cubic maps</a>, Proc. of the Louisiana Conference on Combinatorics, Graph Theory and Computer Science. Vol. 1, (1970), 291-295 [scanned annotated copy].
%H A002010 Christopher Smolen, <a href="https://github.com/chrispbsmolen/almost-cubic-maps">Almost cubic maps: programs, b-files and three computations of the Mullin-Nemeth-Schellenberg table</a>
%H A002010 Jian Zhou, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.03883">Fat and Thin Emergent Geometries of Hermitian One-Matrix Models</a>, arXiv:1810.03883 [math-ph], 2018.
%F A002010 From _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 08 2026: (Start)
%F A002010 a(n) = A002005(n+3) - 10*A002005(n+2) + 18*A002005(n+1) - 10*Sum_{i=0..n+1} A002005(i)*A002005(n+1-i) + 6*Sum_{i=0..n} A002005(i)*A002005(n-i).
%F A002010 G.f.: (C(x) - 1 - 4*x - 32*x^2)/x^3 - 10*(C(x) - 1 - 4*x)/x^2 + 18*(C(x) - 1)/x - 10*(C(x)^2 - 1)/x + 6*C(x)^2, where C(x) is the g.f. of A002005. (End)
%o A002010 (Python)
%o A002010 from math import factorial
%o A002010 def dfact(n):
%o A002010     r = 1
%o A002010     while n > 1: r *= n; n -= 2
%o A002010     return r
%o A002010 def c(n): return 2**(2*n+1)*dfact(3*n)//(factorial(n+2)*dfact(n))  # A002005
%o A002010 def d(n): return sum(c(i)*c(n-i) for i in range(n+1))
%o A002010 def a(n): return c(n+3) - 10*c(n+2) + 18*c(n+1) - 10*d(n+1) + 6*d(n)  # _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 08 2026
%Y A002010 Cf. A002005, A002006, A002007, A002008, A002009.
%K A002010 nonn,changed
%O A002010 0,1
%A A002010 _N. J. A. Sloane_
%E A002010 a(6)-a(7) from Neneth & Schellenberg via _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Sep 08 2026
%E A002010 a(8)-a(17) from _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 08 2026
